      "id": 1,
      "text": "Advance got its name in 1872, chosen to anticipate the growth the Midland Railway would bring to the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Advance%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Wall Street is one of the few streets in town, named after Joe Wall whose family owned over 2,000 acres surrounding Advance until 1971.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Advance%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first settlers arrived in Advance in the 1820s, laying the groundwork for the town that would follow.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Advance%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Advance was officially incorporated in 1858 when residents asked the Indiana General Assembly to recognize the community as a legal town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Advance%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "On May 13, 1995, a tornado struck Advance, causing about $2 million in damage to the town.",
